#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# hp-identity — change what the honeypot's web trap (ports 80 and 443) pretends to be (part of Huginn, AGPL-3.0-or-later).
#
#   hp-identity list              the devices it can pretend to be
#   hp-identity status            what it is now, and when it last changed
#   hp-identity set <id>|random   change now
#   hp-identity rotate            change if ROTATE_DAYS have passed (run by a daily timer)
#
# Settings in /etc/default/hp-identity: ROTATE_DAYS=21 (0 turns the rotation off).
# Each change updates the login page, the Server header and the certificate together and restarts OpenCanary, nothing else.
# The login pages are written from scratch: product names as plain text, no logos or code from any vendor.
# Huginn reads the history through hp-export and cannot change any of this: the honeypot decides by itself.
